<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Repo-pinned NuGet source configuration (issue #186).

  Why this exists:
    Feature 211 committed 38 packages.lock.json files and turned on locked-mode restore in the gate.
    A lockfile records a contentHash per package, so "locked" only means something if every machine
    resolves each package from the SAME source. This repo pinned no nuget.config, so restore
    inherited whatever sources the machine happened to have — the dev container's user-level
    config, a corporate feed, or nothing. `<clear />` ends that: the sources below are the only
    ones, everywhere.

  The local pack-as-you-go feed is NOT a source for this repo (acceptance criterion 2).
    Every project in FS.GG.Rendering.slnx takes its FS.GG.* dependencies (FS.GG.Contracts,
    FS.GG.Game.Core) from nuget.org, and the two in-solution samples (CanvasDemo, SymbologyBoard)
    use ProjectReferences. The out-of-solution samples that DO consume the local feed
    (ControlsGallery, SampleApps, AntShowcase, SecondAntShowcase) each pin their own nuget.config
    with its own `<clear />`, so this file does not reach them.

  packageSourceMapping:
    With one source, mapping does not change which source wins — it changes which sources may be
    consulted AT ALL. The .NET SDK injects its bundled `FSharp/library-packs` folder as an implicit
    restore source (Microsoft.FSharp.NetSdk.targets), and that folder ships an FSharp.Core nupkg
    whose bytes differ from nuget.org's package of the same version. Mapping every pattern to
    nuget.org excludes it, and overrides any packageSourceMapping a developer's user-level config
    defines. Directory.Build.local.props disables that implicit source directly
    (DisableImplicitLibraryPacksFolder); this is the second, source-side guard. Both point the same
    way: FSharp.Core comes from nuget.org, not from whichever SDK patch is installed.
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" protocolVersion="3" />
  </packageSources>

  <packageSourceMapping>
    <packageSource key="nuget.org">
      <package pattern="*" />
    </packageSource>
  </packageSourceMapping>
</configuration>
